<DocsLayout title="Install Haft v9" description="Install the v9 governance substrate without a bundled execution runtime.">
  <h1>Install &amp; init (v9 contract)</h1>

  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/m0n0x41d/haft/main/install.sh | bash

cd /path/to/project
haft init --claude   # or --codex
# restart the host after init</code></pre>

  <p>
    The v9 archive contains the Haft CLI and may contain the independent
    optional <code>haft-embed</code> compatibility sidecar. It contains no
    Open-Sleigh, ERTS, Elixir, or BEAM payload.
  </p>

  <h2>Upgrade safety</h2>

  <ol>
    <li>Stop every host process that can run <code>haft serve</code>.</li>
    <li>Back up the project <code>.haft/</code> directory and its global project ledger.</li>
    <li>Install the exact candidate and record <code>haft version</code> plus its checksum.</li>
    <li>Re-run init for only the host targets you use, then fully restart them.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    A successful v9 installer removes only the managed legacy path
    <code>~/.haft/runtimes/open-sleigh/current</code>. It preserves all
    <code>~/.open-sleigh/</code> data and the independent
    <code>~/.haft/runtimes/haft-embed/</code> tree.
  </p>

  <h2>Removed command migration</h2>

  <p>
    Replace <code>haft run</code> and <code>haft harness</code> automation with
    direct host-agent work or a separately operated runner. The surviving
    integration boundary is <code>haft commission</code> plus the typed
    <code>haft_commission</code> claim, preflight, start, event, and terminal
    lifecycle operations.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/docs/install">Read the full install and rollback notes</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
